{
  "id": "HOS.4",
  "number": "4",
  "bookId": "HOS",
  "reference": "Hosea 4",
  "verseCount": 19,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "4",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "HOS 4"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "4",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hear the word of Jehovah, ye children of Israel; for Jehovah hath a controversy with the inhabitants of the land, because there is no truth, nor goodness, nor knowledge of God in the land. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There is nought but swearing and breaking faith, and killing, and stealing, and committing adultery; they break out, and blood toucheth blood. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore shall the land mourn, and every one that dwelleth therein shall languish, with the beasts of the field and the birds of the heavens; yea, the fishes of the sea also shall be taken away. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet let no man strive, neither let any man reprove; for thy people are as they that strive with the priest. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt stumble in the day, and the prophet also shall stumble with thee in the night; and I will destroy thy mother.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge: because thou hast rejected knowledge, I will also reject thee, that thou shalt be no priest to me: seeing thou hast forgotten the law of thy God, I also will forget thy children. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As they were multiplied, so they sinned against me: I will change their glory into shame. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They feed on the sin of my people, and set their heart on their iniquity. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And it shall be, like people, like priest; and I will punish them for their ways, and will requite them their doings. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they shall eat, and not have enough; they shall play the harlot, and shall not increase; because they have left off taking heed to Jehovah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Whoredom and wine and new wine take away the understanding. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "My people ask counsel at their stock, and their staff declareth unto them; for the spirit of whoredom hath caused them to err, and they have played the harlot, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " from under their God. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They sacrifice upon the tops of the mountains, and burn incense upon the hills, under oaks and poplars and terebinths, because the shadow thereof is good: therefore your daughters play the harlot, and your brides commit adultery. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will not punish your daughters when they play the harlot, nor your brides when they commit adultery; for ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " themselves go apart with harlots, and they sacrifice with the prostitutes; and the people that doth not understand shall be overthrown.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Though thou, Israel, play the harlot, yet let not Judah offend; and come not ye unto Gilgal, neither go ye up to Beth-aven, nor swear, As Jehovah liveth. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For Israel hath behaved himself stubbornly, like a stubborn heifer: now will Jehovah feed them as a lamb in a large place. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ephraim is joined to idols; let him alone. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Their drink is become sour; they play the harlot continually; her rulers dearly love shame. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "HOS 4:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The wind hath wrapped her up in its wings; and they shall be put to shame because of their sacrifices.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "HOS.4.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "HOS.4.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "HOS.5",
    "number": "5",
    "bookId": "HOS"
  },
  "previous": {
    "id": "HOS.3",
